===[ Synthetic data VS Real Data]
The difference is important to understand:

-> 'Real Data': Collected from actual events or observations.
-> 'Synthetic Data': Aritificially generated to resemble real data.
-> 'Augmented data': An 'expanded training' dataset that my combine real
                     and 'synthetic data'.

===[ Typical workflow ]===

            [ Real Dataset: original observations ]
                            |
  [ Generative Model: Learns the underlying data distribution ]
                            |
      [ Synthetic dataset: Aritificially generated observations]
                            |
      [ Augmented dataset: Real and Synthetic data: improved dataset ]


